{"id": "995c741a92cb", "lang": "en", "word": "wolf", "created": "2026-11-08T10:51:06Z", "start": {"stage": "ine-pro", "name": "Proto-Indo-European", "form": "wĺ̥kʷos"}, "end": {"form": "wˈolf", "recorded": "wolf"}, "disabled": ["enm~en:short_o_lowering"], "levels": [{"stage": "ine-pro", "form": "wĺ̥kʷos", "name": "Proto-Indo-European"}, {"stage": "gem-pro", "form": "wˈulfaz", "name": "Proto-Germanic"}, {"stage": "gmw-pro", "form": "wˈolf", "name": "Proto-West Germanic"}, {"stage": "ang", "form": "wˈolf", "name": "Old English"}, {"stage": "enm", "form": "wˈolf", "name": "Middle English"}, {"stage": "en", "form": "wˈolf", "name": "English"}], "laws": [{"step": "ine-pro→gem-pro", "id": "syllabic_l", "name": "Syllabic *l̥ becomes *ul", "tier": "established"}, {"step": "ine-pro→gem-pro", "id": "lkw_to_lp", "name": "Pre-Germanic *kʷ > *p in *-lkʷ-", "tier": "proposed"}, {"step": "ine-pro→gem-pro", "id": "grimm_p", "name": "Grimm: *p > *f after anything but *s", "tier": "established"}, {"step": "ine-pro→gem-pro", "id": "verner_s", "name": "Verner: *s > *z (after unstressed syllable)", "tier": "established"}, {"step": "ine-pro→gem-pro", "id": "o_to_a", "name": "*o merges into *a", "tier": "established"}, {"step": "gem-pro→gmw-pro", "id": "final_z_loss", "name": "Word-final *-z is lost", "tier": "established"}, {"step": "gem-pro→gmw-pro", "id": "u_lowering", "name": "Short *u > *o before *a", "tier": "established"}, {"step": "gem-pro→gmw-pro", "id": "final_a_loss", "name": "Final short *-a is lost", "tier": "established"}], "note": "Middle English ⟨o⟩ here spells /u/, not /ɔ/: wolf, word and wonder write o for u beside the minim letters (w, r, n, m). The vowel is not the short *o that lowered to *ɔ (dog, lot), so short_o_lowering never applied to this word.", "references": ["carney-1994", "scragg-1974"], "default": true}
{"id": "dce9e3c98b81", "lang": "fa", "word": "پرت", "created": "2026-11-08T11:05:48Z", "start": {"stage": "ine-pro", "name": "Proto-Indo-European", "form": "pr̥to"}, "end": {"form": "part", "recorded": "پرت"}, "disabled": ["peo~pal:rt_to_rd"], "levels": [{"stage": "ine-pro", "form": "pr̥to", "name": "Proto-Indo-European"}, {"stage": "iir-pro", "form": "pr̥ta", "name": "Proto-Indo-Iranian"}, {"stage": "ira-pro", "form": "pr̥ta", "name": "Proto-Iranian"}, {"stage": "peo", "form": "parta", "name": "Old Persian"}, {"stage": "pal", "form": "part", "name": "Middle Persian"}, {"stage": "fa", "form": "part", "name": "Persian"}], "laws": [{"step": "ine-pro→iir-pro", "id": "vowel_merger_a", "name": "*e, *o and *a merge as *a", "tier": "established"}, {"step": "ira-pro→peo", "id": "r_syllabic_to_ar", "name": "PIr *r̥ > OP ar", "tier": "established"}, {"step": "peo→pal", "id": "final_vowel_loss", "name": "Final short vowels are lost", "tier": "established"}], "note": "Persian پرت /part/ is recorded with -rt-, so the voicing of *t after *r that gives مرد mard and MP gurdag did not reach this word. The law stays registered for the words that show it; this word says it does not apply.", "references": [], "default": true}
{"id": "7d1b0c7a5e42", "lang": "fa", "word": "گربه", "created": "2026-11-08T14:40:00Z", "start": {"stage": "ine-pro", "name": "Proto-Indo-European", "form": "h₂wl̥pís"}, "end": {"form": "gorbe", "recorded": "گربه"}, "disabled": [], "enabled": ["ine-pro~iir-pro:animal_ka"], "note": "گربه is the root *(H)ulp- 'marten, small predator' plus the Indo-Iranian animal suffix *-ka- (de Vaan 2000, §13: *ul̥.paka-). The suffix is a registered formation law, off for every other word because it adds a syllable; this word's record says it wears it, so the law is switched on here and the ladder climbs from PIE *h₂wl̥pís instead of starting at Proto-Iranian.", "references": ["de-vaan-2000", "wiktionary"], "default": true}
{"id": "b5f3a91c0d67", "lang": "fa", "word": "دیو", "created": "2026-11-08T15:05:00Z", "start": {"stage": "ine-pro", "name": "Proto-Indo-European", "form": "deywós"}, "end": {"form": "dēw", "recorded": "دیو"}, "disabled": ["pal~fa:long_e_to_long_i"], "enabled": [], "note": "دیو is recorded as dēw (Wiktionary: 𐫅𐫏𐫇 dyw /dēw/, /ˈdeːw/), so Middle Persian *ē was not raised to ī in this word, although the general Persian change is ē > ī. The pathway says so instead of silently bending the word.", "references": ["wiktionary"], "default": true}
{"id": "c4a77e2b19d0", "lang": "fa", "word": "دیوانه", "created": "2026-11-08T15:40:00Z", "start": {"stage": "ine-pro", "name": "Proto-Indo-European", "form": "deywós"}, "end": {"form": "dēwˈan", "recorded": "دیوانه"}, "disabled": ["pal~fa:long_e_to_long_i"], "enabled": ["iir-pro~ira-pro:suffix_nah"], "note": "دیوانه is Proto-Iranian *daywánah, analysed by Wiktionary as *daywá- 'demon' plus *-nah, and the record gives /deː.waː.ˈna/ with ē: Middle Persian *ē was not raised to ī in this word, although the general Persian change is ē > ī. The adjective suffix is a registered formation law, off for every word, switched on here because this word's record says it wears it.", "references": ["wiktionary", "hoffmann-forssman-2004"], "default": true}
{"id": "1c3de391a96a", "lang": "fa", "word": "پدر", "created": "2026-11-08T23:59:00Z", "start": {"stage": "ine-pro", "name": "Proto-Indo-European", "form": "ph₂tḗr"}, "end": {"form": "pedar", "recorded": "پدر"}, "disabled": [], "enabled": ["peo~pal:r_stem_oblique"], "levels": [{"stage": "ine-pro", "form": "ph₂tḗr", "name": "Proto-Indo-European"}, {"stage": "iir-pro", "form": "patˈār", "name": "Proto-Indo-Iranian"}, {"stage": "ira-pro", "form": "patˈār", "name": "Proto-Iranian"}, {"stage": "peo", "form": "pitˈār", "name": "Old Persian"}, {"stage": "pal", "form": "pidˈar", "name": "Middle Persian"}, {"stage": "fa", "form": "pedar", "name": "Persian"}], "laws": [{"step": "ine-pro→iir-pro", "id": "syllabic_laryngeals", "name": "Syllabic laryngeals become vowels", "tier": "established"}, {"step": "ine-pro→iir-pro", "id": "long_vowel_merger", "name": "*ē and *ō merge as *ā", "tier": "established"}, {"step": "ira-pro→peo", "id": "anaptyxis_pat", "name": "OP *i for the laryngeal vowel of *patā́-", "tier": "proposed"}, {"step": "peo→pal", "id": "r_stem_oblique", "name": "The r-stem kinship nouns continue their oblique stem: *-tār > MP -tar", "tier": "custom"}, {"step": "peo→pal", "id": "t_to_d", "name": "Intervocalic *-t- > MP *-d-", "tier": "established"}, {"step": "pal→fa", "id": "i_to_e", "name": "MP *i > NP e", "tier": "proposed"}, {"step": "pal→fa", "id": "stress_not_written", "name": "Stress is not written", "tier": "established"}], "note": "پدر 'father' continues Middle Persian pidar (MacKenzie pytl), whose short -a is the oblique stem's vowel, not the long -ā of the Old Persian nominative pitā. The paradigm rule r_stem_oblique states that replacement and is switched off for every other word, because the agent-noun suffix -tār of NP dādār 'creator' keeps its length.", "references": ["kent-1953", "mackenzie-1971", "wiktionary"], "default": true}
